On Wednesday 03 June 2009 03:52:35 tijlan wrote:
> In "da poi broda ca brode", is "ca" part of the poi clause or of the
> main selbri ("brode")?

According to jbofi'e it's part of the poi clause. To make it part of the main 
clause, you can add "vau" after "broda" or "cu" before "ca".

To see how something parses, you can run "jbofihe -t", which gives output like 
this:
| | +-CMAVO : da [KOhA1]
| | | +-CMAVO : poi [NOI]
| | | | +-BRIVLA : broda
| | | | +-CMAVO : ca [PU]
| | | +-BRIDI_TAIL_3
| | +-FULL_RELATIVE_CLAUSE
| +-SUMTI_5
| +-BRIVLA : brode
+-NO_CU_SENTENCE
CHUNKS

